<title>USA: High Plains Wheat - Scattered protection reported.</title>
<headline>High Plains Wheat - Scattered protection reported.</headline>
<dateline>KANSAS CITY, Mo. 1997-06-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>Scattered two to three cents a bushel protection was reported on hard red winter wheat in the Plains ahead of an expected lower opening on KCBT wheat futures.</p>
<p>One Kansas dealer also said he was bidding &quot;basis only.&quot;</p>
<p>News that the U.S. Department of Agriculture had projected spring wheat plantings at a higher-than-expected 19.2 million acres was seen weighing on futures.</p>
<p>Harvest progress of the HRW wheat crop was seen patchy on Monday with rains keeping farmers out of the fields in parts of Kansas and Oklahoma.  </p>
